Package: tampaBayOpenData
Title: An R Interface to Tampa Bay Public Open Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jack", "Lenga", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "jlenga@alumni.cmu.edu",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-1153-8105"))
Description: Discover public 'ArcGIS' layers published by Tampa, St. Petersburg,
    Clearwater, Hillsborough County, Pinellas County, and the Tampa Bay Regional
    Planning Council. The same client can discover other public 'ArcGIS' portals
    and retrieve layers by their REST URLs. A publisher registry configures
    discovery; a separate
    dataset registry identifies layers checked by package maintainers. Filter
    catalogs by source, geometry, topic, category, and modification date.
    Retrieve queryable layers
    with validated pagination, bounded previews, server-side filtering, typed
    tabular results, optional spatial objects, and source provenance. Save large
    downloads as local chunks that can be validated and resumed.
    Public data pages are the City of Tampa GeoHub
    <https://city-tampa.opendata.arcgis.com/>, St. Petersburg ArcGIS portal
    <https://csp.maps.arcgis.com/home/index.html>, Clearwater ArcGIS portal
    <https://cityofclearwater.maps.arcgis.com/home/index.html>, Hillsborough
    County GeoHub <https://hcfl.gov/about-hillsborough/open-data-and-gis/geohub>,
    Pinellas County Enterprise GIS
    <https://new-pinellas-egis.opendata.arcgis.com/>, and Tampa Bay Regional
    Planning Council GeoHub <https://opendata-tbrpc.hub.arcgis.com/>.
